{
  "title": "📈 Geometrical Meaning of Zeroes — Where Graphs Meet the X-axis",
  "hook": "When you throw a ball, its height follows a parabola (a quadratic). The ball starts on the ground, rises, then comes back down. The two points where it touches the ground? Those are the 'zeroes' of the quadratic equation for its height!",
  "explanation": "<div style=\"background:#F3E5F5;border-left:4px solid #7B1FA2;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0\"><strong style=\"color:#7B1FA2\">Zero of a Polynomial:</strong> A number c is a zero of polynomial p(x) if p(c) = 0. Graphically, the zeroes are the x-coordinates where the graph of y = p(x) crosses or touches the x-axis.</div><br><b>Types by Degree:</b><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Type</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Degree</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">General Form</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Max Zeroes</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Graph Shape</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Linear</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">ax + b</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Straight line</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Quadratic</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">ax² + bx + c</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Parabola (U-shape)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Cubic</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">3</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">ax³ + bx² + cx + d</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">3</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">S-curve</td></tr></table><br><b>Quadratic graph cases:</b><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Case</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Graph crosses x-axis</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Number of zeroes</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Example</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Two distinct zeroes</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">At 2 points</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">x² − 5x + 6 → zeroes 2, 3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">One repeated zero</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Touches at 1 point</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1 (repeated)</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">x² − 4x + 4 → zero 2 (twice)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">No real zeroes</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Doesn't cross x-axis</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">0</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">x² + 1 → no real zeroes</td></tr></table><div style=\"background:#FFF8E1;border-left:4px solid #FFB300;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> A polynomial of degree n has <b>at most n</b> zeroes. It can have fewer!</div><svg width=\"260\" height=\"200\" style=\"display:block;margin:10px auto;background:#FAFAFA;border-radius:8px\"><line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"30.0\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"30.0\" y=\"168.44444444444446\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">-1</text><line x1=\"63.33333333333333\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"63.33333333333333\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"96.66666666666666\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"96.66666666666666\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"96.66666666666666\" y=\"168.44444444444446\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">1</text><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"130.0\" y=\"168.44444444444446\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">2</text><line x1=\"163.33333333333331\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"163.33333333333331\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"163.33333333333331\" y=\"168.44444444444446\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">3</text><line x1=\"196.66666666666669\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"196.66666666666669\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"196.66666666666669\" y=\"168.44444444444446\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">4</text><line x1=\"230.0\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"230.0\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"230.0\" y=\"168.44444444444446\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">5</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"170.0\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"55.33333333333333\" y=\"174.0\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">-1</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"154.44444444444446\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"154.44444444444446\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"138.88888888888889\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"138.88888888888889\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"55.33333333333333\" y=\"142.88888888888889\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">1</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"123.33333333333333\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"123.33333333333333\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"55.33333333333333\" y=\"127.33333333333333\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">2</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"107.77777777777779\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"107.77777777777779\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"55.33333333333333\" y=\"111.77777777777779\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">3</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"92.22222222222223\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"92.22222222222223\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"55.33333333333333\" y=\"96.22222222222223\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">4</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"76.66666666666666\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"76.66666666666666\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"55.33333333333333\" y=\"80.66666666666666\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">5</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"61.111111111111114\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"61.111111111111114\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"55.33333333333333\" y=\"65.11111111111111\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">6</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"45.55555555555556\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"45.55555555555556\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"55.33333333333333\" y=\"49.55555555555556\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">7</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"30.0\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"30.0\" stroke=\"#E0E0E0\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"55.33333333333333\" y=\"34.0\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#666\">8</text><text x=\"235\" y=\"158.44444444444446\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">x</text><text x=\"68.33333333333333\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">y</text><line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"-32.22222222222222\" x2=\"63.33333333333333\" y2=\"61.111111111111114\" stroke=\"#4A90D9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"63.33333333333333\" y1=\"61.111111111111114\" x2=\"96.66666666666666\" y2=\"123.33333333333333\" stroke=\"#4A90D9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"96.66666666666666\" y1=\"123.33333333333333\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"154.44444444444446\" stroke=\"#4A90D9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"154.44444444444446\" x2=\"163.33333333333331\" y2=\"154.44444444444446\" stroke=\"#4A90D9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"163.33333333333331\" y1=\"154.44444444444446\" x2=\"196.66666666666669\" y2=\"123.33333333333333\" stroke=\"#4A90D9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"196.66666666666669\" y1=\"123.33333333333333\" x2=\"230.0\" y2=\"61.111111111111114\" stroke=\"#4A90D9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"130.0\" cy=\"154.44444444444446\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#E65100\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"137.0\" y=\"149.44444444444446\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#E65100\">(2,0)</text><circle cx=\"163.33333333333331\" cy=\"154.44444444444446\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#E65100\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"170.33333333333331\" y=\"149.44444444444446\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#E65100\">(3,0)</text><circle cx=\"146.66666666666669\" cy=\"158.33333333333331\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#1565C0\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"153.66666666666669\" y=\"153.33333333333331\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1565C0\">min</text></svg><div style=\"text-align:center;font-size:0.8rem;color:#666\">Graph of x² − 5x + 6: crosses x-axis at x = 2 and x = 3</div>",
  "worked_example": "<b>Example:</b> Find the zeroes of p(x) = x² − 3x − 10 and verify.<br><br><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Factor the polynomial</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">x² − 3x − 10 = (x − 5)(x + 2) [since −5 × 2 = −10, −5 + 2 = −3]</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Set each factor = 0</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">x − 5 = 0 → x = 5;  x + 2 = 0 → x = −2</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Verify x = 5</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">p(5) = 25 − 15 − 10 = 0 ✓</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div><div><strong>Verify x = −2</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">p(−2) = 4 + 6 − 10 = 0 ✓</span></div></div></div><div style=\"background:#F5F5F5;border-left:3px solid #4A90D9;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 12px;margin:6px 0;font-size:0.9rem\">Zeroes are <b>x = 5</b> and <b>x = −2</b>. The graph crosses the x-axis at these two points.</div>",
  "try_this": {
    "question": "Find the zeroes of p(x) = x² − 7x + 12.",
    "hint": "Find two numbers that multiply to 12 and add to −7.",
    "answer": "x² − 7x + 12 = (x − 3)(x − 4). Zeroes: x = 3, x = 4. Verify: p(3) = 9 − 21 + 12 = 0 ✓, p(4) = 16 − 28 + 12 = 0 ✓."
  },
  "fun_fact": "The word 'polynomial' comes from Greek: 'poly' (many) + 'nomos' (term). So it literally means 'many terms'!"
}